{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the 29 October sprint report at head 5c163fdd006385720b524e0c9dee4126d0f1555b, tree 99fc2581d4b295c36c4d72d6bfbbee568eaea919, for request 21eb8ecb and review request 9e12caf6. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nThe head adds one commit to main 25930f62 and one file, `notes/reports/2026-10-29-sprint-report.md`. I read the report and checked its facts against main and the workroom. Most of them hold. Three statements are wrong, and each is a one-line fix.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. The Mac story misnames the kit and the next step.\n   - \"launchd units for the Worker and the celld store\" is wrong. The kit installs three LaunchDaemons: SeaweedFS is the store, celld is the runtime that serves the room Worker, and Caddy serves HTTPS.\n   - \"a shutdown that preserves the store on the same node\" should describe what the witness proves. `down` stops celld before the store, and after the restart every journal reads back entry by entry.\n   - \"the next slice runs the kit on the real machine\" is wrong. All five witnesses already ran on the Mac mini. The next slice is the page stream fallback, which the following paragraph describes.\n2. The boundary-objects story says \"and no item closes\". The note says the opposite: an item's final state ends the item, and it never ends a party's part of the matter. Say that instead.\n3. \"What did not happen\" says that a stray package install dirtied the shared checkout twice, at 11:00 and 16:32, \"from a process outside the workroom\".\n   - It happened three times: at 11:00 and 11:27 with `wrangler ^4.155.0`, and at 16:32 with `^4.156.0`.\n   - At 16:15 a checker helper script also overwrote `apps/room/celld/celld.version` for about a minute. The checker restored the file and reported it in landing check 1bda4259.\n   - No one has identified the process behind the installs, so \"outside the workroom\" is not established. Keep \"the owner is not identified\" and drop that phrase.\n\n## Facts checked and correct\n\n- The eight heads and one direct commit, with the landing times and path counts. For example, `9e313eff` has 132 paths and 90 commits, and 15 of the 41 paths in `1f573145` are under `spikes/typed-surface-before`.\n- The deploy round at 04:33, the three Worker versions, and the claim that the five later landings change no Worker code.\n- Platform has imported the Git package since `c78ef1cb` on 25 October. `scripts/test.mjs` does not list `public-release-modules.test.mjs`, so the gate does not run it.\n- The stream fallback cause matches request 5874b15d.\n- The merge subject of `9e313eff` has 771 code points. My landing check for `2be6ca74` gave 773, which is its length in bytes.\n- The decisions and their rulings, and the four Mac review points in the cost-of-change review.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 25930f62 gives the head tree 99fc2581.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 743 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 25930f62: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 25930f62: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean. No prose line is over 79 characters.\n- The report describes work and quotes no instruction.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The Mac kit's cost-of-change entry leaves out the validation-daemon condition. The evidence met it only as an absence check, and approval 93b6b01d asked the planner for a view on that.\n2. The \"Filed\" table also lists requests filed before this sprint, such as `a53e1464`. Call it \"Requests in this sprint\", or list only the new ones.\n3. The recut landed about 21 hours after the first version, from 20:01 to 16:48, not twenty.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe report changes no code or design. It records the boundaries that the day's landings drew: a host kit outside the Worker, a release plan that matches the source graph, and one commons act. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nThe report holds no credential, key or private path beyond the evidence directories that the notes already name. Item 3 corrects the record of an unreviewed change to the shared checkout. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe report is one file in the established form, at adopter level, with the cost-of-change review for each notable landing. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the report is at adopter level and has the cost-of-change review, and the line-length, link and notes checks pass. Items 1 to 3 need a fix.\n\nA recut that makes items 1 to 3 can come back for a short review of the diff.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e64aa1677961bdb0755ff46a37fd63b08f10d214","binding":"assigned","head":"5c163fdd006385720b524e0c9dee4126d0f1555b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea245fc00bdb58c873203eea999eb831aa3e572f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eb0acdd9f9467d5d71fc9e6ebc2328cd307d5af4\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea245fc00bdb58c873203eea999eb831aa3e572f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}